From: PS3 Custom Toolchain
Subject: [PATCH] libgcc: deregister a frame by its registration, not by its first word (powerpc64-ps3-elf)

EXPERIMENTAL CANDIDATE (not for landing; card t_b90d0462).
__deregister_frame_info treats a BEGIN whose first 32-bit word is zero
as an empty .eh_frame that was never registered, and returns NULL before
looking at the registrations.  For a TABLE registration
(__register_frame_info_table*, __register_frame_table) BEGIN is the
table, whose first element is a pointer: under -mlp64 on this big-endian
target, with every address below 4 GB, its first word is zero, so a table
could never be deregistered - with the list lookup and with the b-tree
alike.  __deregister_frame applied the same test.

With LIBGCC_PS3_DEREGISTER_BY_REGISTRATION (t-ps3-deregister, this
target only) only a null BEGIN is ignored outright; the registration is
searched and removed first under the existing synchronisation.  When
nothing is registered and BEGIN is an empty .eh_frame, the call stays the
no-op it was; a missing NON-empty registration still fails the
assertion.  __deregister_frame frees only the object that comes back.

--- a/libgcc/config.host
+++ b/libgcc/config.host
@@ -1269,7 +1269,7 @@
 	extra_parts="$extra_parts crtbeginS.o crtendS.o crtbeginT.o ecrti.o ecrtn.o ncrti.o ncrtn.o"
 	;;
 powerpc64-ps3-elf*)
-	tmake_file="${tmake_file} rs6000/t-savresfgpr rs6000/t-ps3-crtstuff rs6000/t-ps3-gthreads rs6000/t-ps3-unwind"
+	tmake_file="${tmake_file} rs6000/t-savresfgpr rs6000/t-ps3-crtstuff rs6000/t-ps3-gthreads rs6000/t-ps3-unwind rs6000/t-ps3-deregister"
 	;;
 powerpc64-ps3-kernel-elf*)
 	tmake_file="${tmake_file} rs6000/t-savresfgpr rs6000/t-ps3-crtstuff"
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libgcc/config/rs6000/t-ps3-deregister
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# libgcc frame deregistration for the PS3 LV2 PPU target.
+#
+# Copyright (C) 2026 PS3DK toolchain contributors.
+#
